From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ayn-odin-3: turn off SSC island mode

With island on, s2idle entered right after a sensor close hangs the SoC.

--- a/sensors/config/pakala_power_0.json
+++ b/sensors/config/pakala_power_0.json
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
     ".island":{
       "owner": "power_manager",
       "enable_island":{ "type": "int", "ver": "0",
-        "data": "1"
+        "data": "0"
       }
     }
   }
--- a/sensors/registry/pakala_power_0.json.power.island
+++ b/sensors/registry/pakala_power_0.json.power.island
@@ -1 +1 @@
-{"power.island":{"owner":"power_manager","enable_island":{"type":"int","ver":"0","data":"1"}}}
\ No newline at end of file
+{"power.island":{"owner":"power_manager","enable_island":{"type":"int","ver":"0","data":"0"}}}
\ No newline at end of file
